B.Bk=new A.fS(1,"It is important to treat patients immediately when they require care. Treating patients as they come in, recognizes this idea.",B.di)
B.Bm=new A.fS(2,"It is wrong to discriminate among patients based on characteristics like age. Treating patients as they arrive avoids discrimination based on such characteristics.",B.di)
B.Bg=new A.fS(3,"Treating patients as they arrive, until the last ICU bed is filled, can be an egalitarian way of dividing healthcare, since it is only concerned with immediate need.",B.di)
B.Be=new A.fS(4,"People should not just be treated as they arrive since some people (e.g., with higher social-economic status) may be able to reach hospitals and health services more quickly.",B.ea)
B.Bo=new A.fS(5,"It would be fair to give people who have not had a good shot at a full life (i.e., younger people) priority to maximize everyone's chances at a good life.",B.ea)
B.Bj=new A.fS(6,"If people are treated as they come in, valuable resources are wasted, for instance when patients with a worse prognosis happen to arrive slightly earlier than others.",B.ea)
B.Bl=new A.fS(7,"If one were to prioritize healthcare workers who come in, one might be able to ensure that more people can be rescued and lead full lives.",B.ea)
